From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:41:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Pass how the phone is held on to the call engine

The orientation sent with our picture in a Signal video call said the
front camera's own turn only, so with the phone turned a quarter Android
showed us lying on our side.

The Phone app sends how the phone is held in changeMedia as
deviceOrientation (the shell's quarter turns, 0 top up, 1 left edge up,
2 upside down, 3 right edge up). call.c reads it (call_video_json_turns)
and presage_rust_set_call_turn() passes it through the command channel
(Cmd::SetCallTurn) to call_bridge::set_turn(), which writes "TURN <n>"
to the call's engine, signal-call-media in luneos-synergy-connectors; it
sends it from the next frame on. Given before the engine runs, it is
kept for the call and handed over when the engine starts, as the camera
is.

call_video_json_turns() is tested in test_call_video, turn_command() in
call_video.rs's tests.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
